<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the rational line A, the apotome BD with its annex DC
    // (drawn as the one line BC), the breadth KH with E and F on it, and
    // the line G. Added, all hidden at rest: solid twins BD and DC
    // (initiallyHidden) so the apotome is set out before its annex and DC
    // strokes from D; transparent targets KE, HE, KF, FH, FE (;0;0;0) for
    // the parts of KH the text names. No angles, so no markers. Joyce's
    // page repeats "But BC is greater than BD, therefore KH is also greater
    // than G." as its own paragraph; the deck walks it once.
