            { text: "Since {KH} is to {HE} as {KF} is to {FH}, while {KH} is to {HE} as {HF} is to {FE},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KH","HE","KF","FH","FE"] },
            { text: "therefore {KF} is to {FH} as {HF} is to {FE},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","FH","FE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "KF : FH = HF : FE", ref: "V.11" }] },
            { text: "so that also the first is to the third as the square on the first to the square on the second.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","FE","FH"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "V.Def.9" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {KF} is to {FE} as the square on {KF} is to the square on {FH}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","FE","FH"] },
            { text: "But the square on {KF} is commensurable with the square on {FH},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","FH"] },
            { text: "for {KF} and {FH} are commensurable in square,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","FH"] },
            { text: "therefore {KF} is also commensurable in length with {FE},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","FE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "KF, FE commensurable in length", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "so that {KF} is also commensurable in length with {KE}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","KE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "KF, KE commensurable in length", ref: "X.15" }] },
            { text: "But {KE} is rational and commensurable in length with {BC},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KE","BC"] },
            { text: "therefore {KF} is also rational and commensurable in length with {BC}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","BC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "KF rational, commensurable with BC", ref: "X.12" }] },
            { text: "Since {BC} is to {CD} as {KF} is to {FH}, alternately, {BC} is to {KF} as {DC} is to {FH}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","DC","KF","FH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "BC : KF = DC : FH", ref: "V.16" }] },
            { text: "But {BC} is commensurable with {KF}, therefore {FH} is also commensurable in length with {CD}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","KF","FH","DC"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FH, CD commensurable in length", ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "But {BC} and {CD} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","DC"] },
            { text: "therefore {KF} and {FH} are also rational straight lines commensurable in square only.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","FH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "KF, FH rational", ref: "X.Def.I.3" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {KH} is binomial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KH"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "KH binomial", ref: "X.36" }] },
            { text: "If now the square on {BC} is greater than the square on {CD}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","DC"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line commensurable with {BC},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC"] },
            { text: "then the square on {KF} is also greater than the square on {FH}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","FH"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line commensurable with {KF}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.14" }] },
            { text: "And, if {BC} is commensurable in length with the rational straight line set out, then {KF} is also;",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","KF"] },
            { text: "if {CD} is commensurable in length with the rational straight line set out, then {FH} is also;",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DC","FH"] },
            { text: "but, if neither of the straight lines {BC} nor {CD}, then neither of the straight lines {KF} nor {FH}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","DC","KF","FH"] },
            { text: "But, if the square on {BC} is greater than the square on {CD}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","DC"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {BC},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC"] },
            { text: "then the square on {KF} is also greater than the square on {FH}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","FH"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {KF}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.14" }] },
            { text: "And, if {BC} is commensurable with the rational straight line set out, then {KF} is also;",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","KF"] },
            { text: "if {CD} is so commensurable, then {FH} is also;",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DC","FH"] },
            { text: "but, if neither of the straight lines {BC} nor {CD}, then neither of the straight lines {KF} nor {FH}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BC","DC","KF","FH"] },
            { text: "Therefore {KH} is a binomial straight line, the terms of which {KF} and {FH}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KH","KF","FH"] },
            { text: "are commensurable with the terms {BC} and {CD} of the apotome and in the same ratio,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","FH","BC","DC"] },
            { text: "and further, {KH} has the same order as {BD}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KH","BD"] },
            { text: "Therefore, the square on a rational straight line, if applied to an apotome,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["A","BD"] },
            { text: "produces as breadth the binomial straight line",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KH"] },
            { text: "the terms of which are commensurable with the terms of the apotome and in the same ratio;",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KF","FH","BC","DC"] },
            { text: "and further the binomial so arising has the same order as the apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["KH","BD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
